'''Logosbook''' is a spell that allows the caster to communicate with another Seeker using a book. One Seeker writes in the book, and the message appears in the other book.

== History ==
Logosbook was used by [[Zhalia Moon]] to enchant journals owned by herself and [[Dante Vale]] when she went undercover as a [[Silent Soldier]] initiate so she could inform him of the activities of the [[Blood Spiral]]. {{source|Zhalia's Mission}}

After [[Den Fears]] and [[Lok Lambert]] were attacked by [[Tantras]]' students in the Streets of Venice, [[Zhalia Moon|Zhalia]] used Logosbook to inform [[Dante Vale|Dante]] that the [[Blood Spiral|Spirals]] were looking for Den. Later, Dante gets a hunch and decides to check his book, reading Zhalia's message and deciding to face Tantras head-on. {{Source|Boys Will Be Seekers}}

With the Blood Spiral army approaching the [[Fortress of Iron Will]], Zhalia used the spell to inform Dante. He shortly used Logosbook himself to receive her message. {{source|Sophie on Trial}}

On the longest night of the year, Zhalia used the spell to inform Dante of the location of the [[Spiral Mark]] on the Siberian Plateau. {{source|Words from Eathon}}

With Dante seemingly sacrificing himself to stop the impact of the [[Red Comet]], he had written a message to Zhalia using Logosbook, saying "You can't get rid of me that easily". As all hope seemed lost in the fight against [[the Betrayer]], Zhalia remembered Dante decided to check her book, reading the message. This prompted [[Umbra]] to teleport to her location, bringing back Dante's ashes. This allowed him to revive after using [[Copykind]] to mimic [[Phoenix]]'s ability to rise from the ashes. {{Source|Dante's Return}}

